# ORIGINAL: THE PIN — the upstream commit the ports cite, and the oracle every live differential is
# judged against, locally AND in CI: ONE commit (user, 2026-10-11).
#
#   version:  what `swipl --version` says
#   commit:   the swipl-devel commit — the ported files' `# UPSTREAM: … @ <commit>` headers cite it
#             (tools/port_check.jl), and the oracle is a BUILD OF IT (tools/build_oracle.sh, the
#             same recipe here and in CI, cached there by commit + build flags)
#   sync-from: present only DURING a sync: the previous pin, which a ported file's header may
#             still cite until its upstream changes are ported. The sync's last commit removes the
#             line, and from then on every header is at `commit`.
#
# EVERY GATE ASSERTS IT WHERE IT RUNS (tools/lib_evidence.sh `_check_swipl_pin`, tools/swipl_pin.jl:
# the runner, each evidence worker, the warm daemon, CI's analysis job): `swipl --version` is
# `version`, and the binary's `version_git` flag — `<version>-<n>-g<sha>`, written into a build
# from a git checkout — names `commit`. A release binary has no such flag and is refused: the
# oracle and the ported source cannot drift apart.
#
# HISTORY. Until 2026-10-11 the pin was a version alone, 10.1.16: the local oracle was a build of
# bae881a2 and CI ran inside the official image `swipl:10.1.16`, the release 20 commits earlier
# (one of them in src/, outside every ported file). A release moved CI's oracle once, mid-port
# (10.1.17 on the devel PPA, 2026-10-04), which is why CI's oracle is fixed.
# BUMP RULE: the pin, the local build and CI's build move TOGETHER, as a scheduled step with the
# drift report (tools/upstream_drift.jl) and every differential rerun — never to turn a red run
# green. The 2026-10-11 sync: bae881a2 → ac807ba8 (72 commits; 17 ported upstream files changed,
# the fourteen fixes of docs/upstream_reports.md among them) — finished the same day: every header
# is at `commit` and no `sync-from:` line is left.
# The 2026-10-13 mini-sync: ac807ba8 → 8609e216 (26 commits, 10 of them in src/ or boot/; ONE
# commit here, so no `sync-from:` line was ever written): pl-comp.c's two fixes for a first-occurrence
# variable under `\+` in a branch of `;` (7dba157e, 27c742f0) ported, the kernel's own defensive
# initialisation of those variables removed with them; the others touch no ported function
# (docs/architecture.md, the pin's section).
